; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Star Shapes
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     star, angles, filled, repeat
; SUMMARY:  Draws pointy stars with crossing lines, an outline star with no lines inside, and a filled gold star.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The top row shows stars where the lines cross in the middle:
;   5 points, 7 points and 8 points. The bottom row shows a star
;   drawn round its outside edge only, and the same star painted
;   gold like a sheriff's badge.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try  star5 200  in the command center.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a 5 point star turns 144 degrees, and goes round the center TWICE
;   * two turns in a row (a left and a right) can make zigzag edges
;   * FILLED paints the inside of the path the turtle walks
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * In STAR5 change 144 to 150 or 170. What do you see?
;   * Make OUTLINESTAR with 6 or 9 points instead of 5.
;   * Change the gold color to [200 0 0] for a red star.
; ============================================================

; Five lines, each turn 144 degrees. 5 x 144 = 720, which is two
; full turns: the turtle circles the middle twice before it gets home.
to star5 :size
  repeat 5 [forward :size right 144]
end

; A 7 point star skips over 3 points at a time.
; The turn is 3 / 7 of a full circle.
to star7 :size
  repeat 7 [forward :size right 360 * 3 / 7]
end

; An 8 point star turns 135 degrees, three eighths of a turn.
to star8 :size
  repeat 8 [forward :size right 135]
end

; An outline star: walk out to a tip, turn sharply, walk back in,
; turn a little the other way. Out-and-in, five times.
; Each time round it turns 144 right and 72 left, 72 degrees in all,
; and 5 x 72 = 360, so the turtle comes home facing the right way.
to outlinestar :edge
  repeat 5 [
    forward :edge
    right 144
    forward :edge
    left 72
  ]
end

to jumpto :x :y :heading
  penup setxy :x :y setheading :heading pendown
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3

; top row: stars with crossing lines
setpencolor 1
jumpto -330 80 18
star5 150
setpencolor 13
jumpto -70 80 13
star7 150
setpencolor 4
jumpto 210 70 22.5
star8 150

; bottom row: outline star, then a filled one
setpencolor 2
jumpto -220 -170 18
outlinestar 70

setpencolor [180 120 0]
jumpto 100 -170 18
filled [255 210 40] [outlinestar 70]
hideturtle
